---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import { scope, registry, manifest, href } from '../../lib/catalogue';
import { familyAvailability, priorityLabels } from '../../lib/scope';
import { Content as ScopePolicy } from '../../../docs/scope.md';
const families = scope.modules.flatMap(module => module.families);
const publishedIds = new Set(manifest.datasets.map(dataset => dataset.id));
const byId = new Map(registry.series.map(series => [series.id, series]));
const outstanding = scope.deferred_series.filter(item => !publishedIds.has(item.series_id));
---
<Layout title="Scope and roadmap" description={scope.statement}>
  <section class="page-heading"><div class="eyebrow">SCOPE & ROADMAP</div><h1 class="detail-title">The history of<br /><em>Swiss prosperity.</em></h1><p>{scope.statement}</p></section>
  <aside class="scope-summary" aria-label="Scope and publication status"><div><strong>{scope.modules.length}</strong><span>thematic modules</span></div><div><strong>{families.length}</strong><span>indicator families in scope</span></div><div><strong>{manifest.datasets.length}</strong><span>{process.env.HEI_DEMO === '1' ? 'production datasets in this demo' : 'published datasets'}</span></div><p>Families group related views; they are not dataset counts. This is the governing scope and acquisition plan. Planned entries have no published observations.</p></aside>
  <nav class="topic-nav scope-nav" aria-label="Scope sections"><a href="#priorities">Next additions</a><a href="#modules">Ten modules</a><a href="#outstanding">Unresolved datasets</a><a href="#governance">Scope policy</a></nav>
  <aside class="notice"><div><strong>Wage and household-income priority completed</strong><p><a href="#family-real-wages">Real wage purchasing power</a> (1942–2025) and <a href="#family-disposable-income">real median disposable household income</a> (2000–2023) are now published with their different definitions and historical breaks. The maintained foundation also includes <a href="#family-bilateral-fx">CHF bilateral exchange rates</a>, <a href="#family-effective-fx">nominal and real effective exchange rates</a>, <a href="#family-hourly-productivity">output per hour worked</a> and <a href="#family-hours-worked">total hours worked</a>. Housing and its financing now lead the remaining priorities.</p></div></aside>
  <section id="priorities" class="details"><h2>What to add next</h2><p>Maintain and correct the verified foundation first. The next acquisitions close the missing connections between production, households, financing and the external economy.</p><ol class="scope-priorities">{scope.acquisition_order.map(group => <li><h3>{group.title}</h3><p>{group.why}</p><p>{group.family_ids.map((id, index) => <>{index > 0 && ' · '}<a href={`#family-${id}`}>{families.find(family => family.id === id)!.title}</a></>)}</p></li>)}</ol><p class="muted"><strong>P1:</strong> next acquisitions above. <strong>P2:</strong> employment, migration, distribution, structural change and monetary/financial context. <strong>P3:</strong> deeper balance sheets, investment returns and comparisons. Priorities guide acquisition; source verification determines publication.</p></section>
  <section id="modules" class="details"><h2>Ten thematic modules</h2><p>Browse each module for its historical question, existing observations and remaining work. Availability is calculated from published datasets; native-frequency downloads do not automatically become annual charts.</p><div class="scope-modules">{scope.modules.map((module, index) => <details id={`module-${module.id}`} class="scope-module"><summary><span class="scope-module-number">{String(index + 1).padStart(2, '0')}</span><span><strong>{module.title}</strong><small>{module.families.length} indicator families · {module.families.filter(family => familyAvailability(family, publishedIds) !== 'Planned').length} with published data</small></span></summary><div class="scope-module-content"><p class="scope-question">{module.question}</p><a href={href(`series/#topic-${module.id}`)}>View catalogue module →</a>{module.families.map(family => <article id={`family-${family.id}`} class="scope-family" data-scope-priority={family.priority}><header><h3>{family.title}</h3><span class="badge">{familyAvailability(family, publishedIds)}</span><span class="badge">{priorityLabels[family.priority]}</span></header><p>{family.annual_view}</p><p><strong>Next step:</strong> {family.next_step}</p>{family.series_ids.length > 0 ? <ul>{family.series_ids.map(id => <li><a href={href(`series/${id}/`)}>{byId.get(id)!.title} →</a> <span class="scope-series-status">{publishedIds.has(id) ? 'Published' : 'Candidate · no public observations'}</span></li>)}</ul> : <p class="muted">Planned family · source selection and verification required.</p>}</article>)}</div></details>)}</div></section>
  <section id="outstanding" class="details"><h2>Existing unresolved datasets</h2><p>These definitions already exist. They are separate from the new P1 acquisitions. The annual GMBF series is available; individual auctions add later detail. Market-index variants follow the core prosperity indicators.</p><div class="scope-outstanding">{outstanding.map(item => <article><h3><a href={href(`series/${item.series_id}/`)}>{byId.get(item.series_id)!.title} →</a></h3><span class="badge">P3 · {item.blocker}</span><p>{item.next_step}</p></article>)}</div><p class="muted">The empty historical-SNB-instruments entry is a structural reference. Its individual instruments are published and it is excluded from the unresolved-dataset count.</p><a href="https://www.six-group.com/en/market-data/indices/licensing.html">SIX licensing and access information ↗</a></section>
  <section id="governance" class="details"><h2>How the scope governs the atlas</h2><p>The main view is annual, centred on 1946–2026, with different starting dates for different series. Selected nineteenth-century, international and cantonal views are later extensions. A curated six-panel overview is the target as the required data becomes available; the current workspace starts empty.</p><p>Historical events and institutional regimes form a parallel evidence layer. Decisions, effective dates and interpretations require their own sources. Co-movement helps formulate questions; it does not establish causation.</p><details class="scope-policy"><summary>Read the full governing scope and admission rules</summary><div class="scope-policy-content"><ScopePolicy /></div></details><p class="muted"><a href="https://github.com/duracell04/swiss-economic-atlas/blob/main/docs/scope.md">Read the scope in the repository ↗</a> · <a href={href('methodology/#publication')}>Publication standards →</a></p></section>
</Layout>
<script>
  function revealFamily() {
    if (!location.hash.startsWith('#family-')) return;
    const family = document.getElementById(location.hash.slice(1));
    const module = family?.closest('details');
    if (module) { module.open = true; family?.scrollIntoView({ block: 'start' }); }
  }
  addEventListener('hashchange', revealFamily);
  revealFamily();
</script>
